From da31f8bf11165c5f686da26bdeb0fc0daf514c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alena Rybakina <a.rybakina@postgrespro.ru>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 23:09:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add machinery for grabbing extended vacuum statistics

Vacuum statistics are stored separately from regular relation and
database statistics. Dedicated PGSTAT_KIND_VACUUM_RELATION and
PGSTAT_KIND_VACUUM_DB entries in the cumulative statistics system
allocate memory for vacuum-specific metrics. Statistics are gathered
separately for tables and indexes according to vacuum phases. The
ExtVacReport union and type field distinguish PGSTAT_EXTVAC_TABLE vs
PGSTAT_EXTVAC_INDEX. Heap vacuum stats are sent to the cumulative
statistics system after vacuum has processed the indexes. Database
vacuum statistics aggregate per-table and per-index statistics within
the database.

Statistics are exposed only via the ext_vacuum_statistics extension,
which registers set_report_vacuum_hook. When the hook is set, vacuum
gathers extended stats and passes them to the hook; otherwise no extra
overhead is incurred.

Common for tables, indexes, and database:
- total_blks_hit, total_blks_read, total_blks_dirtied: hit, miss, and
  dirtied pages in shared buffers during a vacuum operation
  (total_blks_dirtied counts only pages dirtied by this vacuum)
- blk_read_time, blk_write_time: access and flush time for buffer
  pages (blk_write_time can stay zero if no flushes occurred)
- total_time: wall-clock time from start to finish, including idle
  time (I/O and lock waits)
- delay_time: total vacuum sleep time in vacuum delay points

Table and index:
- tuples_deleted: tuples removed by the vacuum operation
- pages_removed: pages by which relation storage was reduced
- pages_deleted: freed pages (file size may remain unchanged)

These are independent of WAL and buffer stats and are not summed at
the database level.

Table only:
- pages_frozen: pages marked all-frozen in the visibility map
- pages_all_visible: pages marked all-visible in the visibility map
- wraparound_failsafe_count: number of urgent anti-wraparound vacuums

Table and database:
- wraparound_failsafe: count of urgent anti-wraparound cleanups

Database only:
- errors: number of error-level errors caught during vacuum

